completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Git tag: `v1.4.7`\r\nInstallation method: `cmake v3.24.2`\r\nPlatform: Ubuntu 18.04\r\n\r\nInstall steps:\r\n```\r\ngit clone https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK.git\r\ncd MAVSDK\r\ngit checkout v1.4.7\r\ngit submodule update --init --recursive\r\n/snap/bin/cmake -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug -Bbuild/default -H.\r\n/snap/bin/cmake --build build/default -j8\r\nsudo /snap/bin/cmake --build build/default --target install\r\n```\r\n\r\nUsage in CMakeLists.txt:\r\n```\r\nfind_package(MAVSDK 1.4.7 REQUIRED)\r\ntarget_link_libraries(... PRIVATE MAVSDK::mavsdk)\r\n```\r\n\r\nUsage in my_header.h:\r\n```\r\n#include <mavsdk/mavsdk.h>\r\n#include <mavsdk/plugins/mavlink_passthrough/mavlink_passthrough.h>\r\n```\r\n\r\nCompilation error:\r\n```\r\nIn file included from /usr/local/include/mavsdk/plugins/mavlink_passthrough/mavlink_passthrough.h:8:0,\r\n                 from /home/me/project/my_header.h:17,\r\n/usr/local/include/mavsdk/plugins/mavlink_passthrough/mavlink_include.h:3:10: fatal error: mavlink/v2.0/common/mavlink.h: No such file or directory\r\n #include \"mavlink/v2.0/common/mavlink.h\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nFirst few lines of mavlink_passthrough.h:\r\n```\r\n#pragma once\r\n\r\n#include <memory>\r\n#include <string>\r\n#include <functional>\r\n\r\n// This plugin provides/includes the mavlink 2.0 header files.\r\n#include \"mavlink_include.h\"\r\n#include \"mavsdk/plugin_base.h\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nUnless I'm including the wrong file in my header, it seems like `#include \"mavlink_include.h\"` should be `#include \"mavsdk/mavlink_include.h\"` instead so that the linker (?) can find the header based on standard system include paths. I made this change locally and it resolved my issue, but this should be handled on the source-code end.\r\n\r\nOtherwise, am I including `MavlinkPassthrough` incorrectly?\r\n\r\nThanks!", "closed_by": 